old [&_strong]:text-text [&_ul]:mb-2.5 [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-5 [&_ol]:mb-2.5 [&_ol]:list-decimal [&_ol]:pl-5 [&_li]:mb-1 [&_code]:rounded [&_code]:bg-bg [&_code]:px-1 [&_code]:py-0.5 [&_code]:font-mono [&_code]:text-[11px] [&_code]:text-text [&_table]:mb-3 [&_table]:w-full [&_table]:text-left [&_table]:text-[11.5px] [&_th]:border-b [&_th]:border-border [&_th]:pb-1 [&_th]:pr-3 [&_th]:font-semibold [&_th]:text-text [&_td]:border-b [&_td]:border-border [&_td]:py-1 [&_td]:pr-3 [&_td]:align-top [&_a]:text-teal hover:[&_a]:underline [&_blockquote]:border-l-2 [&_blockquote]:border-border2 [&_blockquote]:pl-3 [&_blockquote]:italic","children":[["$","h1","h1-0",{"children":"Transaction Costs in Indian F&O"}],"\n",["$","p","p-0",{"children":"Costs are not a rounding error in Indian derivatives. On short-dated,\r\nmulti-leg, narrow-width structures they can exceed the theoretical edge\r\nentirely. This lesson covers what is charged and on what base — the base\r\nmatters more than the rate."}],"\n",["$","p","p-1",{"children":["$","em","em-0",{"children":"STT rates verified 24 July 2026 against broker billing schedules. They changed\r\non 1 April 2026 and will change again by Finance Act."}]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-0",{"children":"Securities Transaction Tax"}],"\n",["$","p","p-2",{"children":"STT is the largest statutory component and the one with the most\r\ncounter-intuitive structure."}],"\n",["$","table","table-0",{"children":[["$","thead","thead-0",{"children":["$","tr","tr-0",{"children":[["$","th","th-0",{"children":"Segment"}],["$","th","th-1",{"children":"Rate"}],["$","th","th-2",{"children":"Levied on"}],["$","th","th-3",{"children":"Side"}]]}]}],["$","tbody","tbody-0",{"children":[["$","tr","tr-0",{"children":[["$","td","td-0",{"children":"Equity delivery"}],["$","td","td-1",{"children":"0.1%"}],["$","td","td-2",{"children":"Turnover"}],["$","td","td-3",{"children":"Both buy and sell"}]]}],["$","tr","tr-1",{"children":[["$","td","td-0",{"children":"Equity intraday"}],["$","td","td-1",{"children":"0.025%"}],["$","td","td-2",{"children":"Turnover"}],["$","td","td-3",{"children":"Sell only"}]]}],["$","tr","tr-2",{"children":[["$","td","td-0",{"children":"Futures"}],["$","td","td-1",{"children":"0.05%"}],["$","td","td-2",{"children":"Traded price"}],["$","td","td-3",{"children":"Sell only"}]]}],["$","tr","tr-3",{"children":[["$","td","td-0",{"children":"Options — sold"}],["$","td","td-1",{"children":"0.15%"}],["$","td","td-2",{"children":["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Premium"}]}],["$","td","td-3",{"children":"Sell only"}]]}],["$","tr","tr-4",{"children":[["$","td","td-0",{"children":"Options — exercised"}],["$","td","td-1",{"children":"0.15%"}],["$","td","td-2",{"children":["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Intrinsic value"}]}],["$","td","td-3",{"children":"Buyer, on exercise"}]]}]]}]]}],"\n",["$","p","p-3",{"children":"Rates on futures and options were raised effective 1 April 2026 — futures from\r\n0.02%, options sold from 0.1%, options exercised from 0.125%. Equity delivery\r\nand intraday were left unchanged."}],"\n",["$","h3","h3-0",{"children":"The exercised-option trap"}],"\n",["$","p","p-4",{"children":"The two option rows have the same rate and completely different bases, and this\r\nis the single most expensive avoidable cost in Indian options."}],"\n",["$","p","p-5",{"children":["An option that is ",["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"sold"}]," pays 0.15% of the ",["$","em","em-0",{"children":"premium"}],". An option that is\r\n",["$","strong","strong-1",{"children":"exercised"}]," pays 0.15% of the ",["$","em","em-1",{"children":"intrinsic value"}]," — the full in-the-money\r\namount, which for a deep in-the-money option is many multiples of the premium\r\noriginally paid."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-6",{"children":"Consider a call bought for a small premium that finishes deep in the money.\r\nSquaring off in the market pays STT on the sale premium. Allowing it to be\r\nexercised at expiry pays STT on the entire intrinsic value. The difference can\r\nbe larger than the profit on the position."}],"\n",["$","p","p-7",{"children":"The general shape: an in-the-money option left to expire is charged on a much\r\nlarger base than the same option closed in the market. This applies to index\r\noptions at cash settlement as well as to stock options."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-1",{"children":"Everything else"}],"\n",["$","p","p-8",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Exchange transaction charges"}]," — a small percentage of premium turnover for\r\noptions, of contract turnover for futures. Rates differ between NSE and BSE and\r\nbetween segments."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-9",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Stamp duty"}]," — levied on the buy side only, at rates set per segment."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-10",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"SEBI turnover fees"}]," — a very small levy on turnover."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-11",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"GST"}]," — 18%, charged on brokerage plus exchange transaction charges (not on\r\nSTT, and not on turnover directly)."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-12",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Brokerage"}]," — the only negotiable component. Typically a flat per-order\r\namount for derivatives rather than a percentage, which is what makes leg count\r\nmatter."]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-2",{"children":"Why leg count dominates"}],"\n",["$","p","p-13",{"children":"For flat-fee brokerage, cost scales with the number of orders, not the size of\r\nthe position."}],"\n",["$","table","table-1",{"children":[["$","thead","thead-0",{"children":["$","tr","tr-0",{"children":[["$","th","th-0",{"children":"Structure"}],["$","th","th-1",{"children":"Legs"}],["$","th","th-2",{"children":"Orders round-trip"}]]}]}],["$","tbody","tbody-0",{"children":[["$","tr","tr-0",{"children":[["$","td","td-0",{"children":"Long call"}],["$","td","td-1",{"children":"1"}],["$","td","td-2",{"children":"2"}]]}],["$","tr","tr-1",{"children":[["$","td","td-0",{"children":"Vertical spread"}],["$","td","td-1",{"children":"2"}],["$","td","td-2",{"children":"4"}]]}],["$","tr","tr-2",{"children":[["$","td","td-0",{"children":"Straddle / strangle"}],["$","td","td-1",{"children":"2"}],["$","td","td-2",{"children":"4"}]]}],["$","tr","tr-3",{"children":[["$","td","td-0",{"children":"Iron condor / butterfly"}],["$","td","td-1",{"children":"4"}],["$","td","td-2",{"children":"8"}]]}]]}]]}],"\n",["$","p","p-14",{"children":"An iron condor pays four times the brokerage of a long call for the same\r\nnotional. On a wide condor in a liquid contract that is immaterial. On a narrow\r\none it can be a substantial fraction of the maximum profit — and narrow\r\nstructures are exactly the ones with small maximum profits."}],"\n",["$","p","p-15",{"children":["The ratio worth computing before entry is ",["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"total round-trip cost divided by\r\nmaximum profit"}],". For narrow defined-risk structures this ratio is often\r\ndouble-digit percentage, and it is fixed at entry regardless of how the\r\nposition performs."]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-3",{"children":"Bid-ask spread is a cost too"}],"\n",["$","p","p-16",{"children":"Not a charge, but a real one. Crossing the spread on entry and exit is paid on\r\nevery leg. In liquid NIFTY weekly strikes near the money the spread is narrow.\r\nIn monthly-only indices, in far strikes, and in single-stock options it can be\r\nwide enough to dominate every statutory charge combined."}],"\n",["$","p","p-17",{"children":"Since the November 2024 rationalisation removed weekly contracts from\r\nBANKNIFTY, FINNIFTY, MIDCPNIFTY and NIFTYNXT50, liquidity in those chains\r\nconcentrated into monthly expiries — so far-strike liquidity in them is thinner\r\nthan pre-2024 material suggests."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-4",{"children":"Related"}],"\n",["$","ul","ul-0",{"children":["\n",["$","li","li-0",{"children":[["$","code","code-0",{"children":"india-market-structure/physical-settlement.md"}]," — the other expiry-day cost"]}],"\n",["$","li","li-1",{"children":[["$","code","code-0",{"children":"risk/expectancy.md"}]," — where costs enter the arithmetic"]}],"\n",["$","li","li-2",{"children":[["$","code","code-0",{"children":"strategies/volatility/iron-condor.md"}]," — the most cost-sensitive structure here"]}],"\n"]}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-[10px] leading-relaxed text-faint","children":["Educational material describing how a structure behaves. Not a recommendation, not a signal, and not personalised advice. Source: ",["$","code",null,{"className":"font-mono","children":"docs/learning/india-market-structure/transaction-costs.md"}]]}]]}],null],null],null]},[null,["$","$L3",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","(workspace)","children","learning","children","strategy","children","$4","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":"$undefined","template":["$","$L5",null,{}],"templateStyles":"$undefined","templateScripts":"$undefined","notFound":"$undefined","notFoundStyles":"$undefined"}]],null]},[null,["$","$L3",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","(workspace)","children","learning","children","strategy","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":"$undefined","template":["$","$L5",null,{}],"templateStyles":"$undefined","templateScripts":"$undefined","notFound":"$undefined","notFoundStyles":"$undefined"}]],null]},[null,["$","$L3",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","(workspace)","children","learning","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":"$undefined","template":["$","$L5",null,{}],"templateStyles":"$undefined","templateScripts":"$undefined","notFound":"$undefined","notFoundStyles":"$undefined"}]],null]},[[null,["$","$L6",null,{"children":["$","$L3",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","(workspace)","children"],"er